==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|gler}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*glasą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰel-||to shine, glimmer, glow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/klɛːr/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛːr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|glers|gler}}

# [[glass]] {{gloss|substance made by melting sand}}
# {{label|is|geology|physics}} glass {{gloss|amorphous solid material}}
# a glass [[bottle]]
# [[pane]] of glass
# [[lens]]
# a flat, slippery surface covering made of [[ice]] (e.g. a frozen pond surface or frozen surface water on a road)
# {{label|is|in the plural}} pieces, shards of glass

